      <div type="clause" n="11.5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 11.5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11.5" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="56" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif borenran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.star3"/> wifmen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.20"/> ðis gelimpe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.21"/>, weaxe sio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.15"/> bót be ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.22"/> were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11.5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="56" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif þis <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.star"/>borenran wifmen gelimpe, weaxe seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.8"/> bot be ðam were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11.5" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf borenran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.star-2"/> wifm<hi rend="italic">en</hi> þis g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>limpe, wexe seo bót be ðam were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="11.5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Si hoc in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.20-2"/> nobilius oriunda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.21-2"/> muliere contingat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.22-2"/>, crescat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.23"/> emendatio, sicut eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.24"/> natalis ingenuitas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.11"/> erit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.oe.25"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="70" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif borenran<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Af_11-5.attnote.fn.14"/> wifmen ðis gelimpe, weaxe<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#Af_11-5.attnote.fn.15"/> sio bót be ðam were.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="13.5" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="308" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif borenran wifmen ðis gelimpe, weaxe sio bót be ðam were.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="57" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn einer mehr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.de.1"/> [als gemeinfrei] geborenen Jungfrau dies [Verletzen ihrer Keuschheit] geschieht, so wachse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_11-5.lnote.de.2"/> die [ihr zustehende] Busse je nach dem Wergeld [derselben].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If this [violation of her chastity] happens to a more highly born woman [than common free], let the [compensation due to her] grow according to [her] wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="71" ed="#attenborough"/>If this [outrage] is done to a woman of higher birth<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_11-5.attnote.n.1"/>, the compensation to be paid shall increase according to the wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="309" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If this happens to a [nobly] born woman, let the compensation increase according to the <hi rend="italic">wer</hi>.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="309"><label>cf. (term)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_34">Ine 34</ref> <quote>Cf. Ine §34 deorborenran "nobly born."</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æþelborenran <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi> [<hi rend="italic">vgl. Quadrip.</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æþelborenran So Ld [cf. Quadrip.]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-man <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-man So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gelympe <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gelympe So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seo <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seo Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">bett <hi rend="italic">über der Zeile</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">bett above the line</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ignob. <hi rend="italic">st.</hi> in n. <hi rend="italic">T Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ignob. instead of in n. T Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.21-2" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ortalium <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ortalium K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.22-2" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tigerit <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tigerit Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eius <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hk Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eius added by Hk Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">n. e. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">n. e. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">erat <hi rend="italic">Hk Brti; folgt c.</hi> 18 — 18, 3 <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erat Hk Brti; cap. 18 — 18, 3 follows in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.oe.star-2" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">davor</hi> æðel <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æðel written above before it in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">borenran</hi> ist archetyp laut EHB. Synonym mit <hi rend="italic">boren</hi> von derselben Wurzel ist das Adj. <hi rend="italic">byrde</hi> (‘of high rank’ Sweet <hi rend="italic">Ags. reader;</hi> ‘born’ Bosw.-Toller), das Ælfred ebenfalls kompariert: ‘jeder zahlt <hi rend="italic">be hys gebyrdum, se byrdesta</hi> muss 75 zahlen’; <hi rend="italic">Oros.</hi> ed. Sweet 18. Auch mhd. <hi rend="italic">geboren</hi> gewinnt den Sinn ‘adlig, ebenbürtig’. — Das 11. Jh. nahm an dem Worte Anstoss; ‘besser geboren’ ändert H cor., also mit doppeltem Komparativ, ‘mehr edelgeboren’ So Ld und vielleicht Q’s Vorlage. Letzteres nahmen, da <hi rend="italic">æðelboren</hi> häufig vorkommt, frühere Editoren in den Text. — Möglicherweise schrieb Af wie Ine 34, 1 <hi rend="italic">deorborenran,</hi> und übersah Archetyp, durch gleiches <hi rend="italic">-or</hi> verleitet, die ersten 4 Buchstaben</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">borenran</hi> is the reading of the archetype, according to EHB. Synonymous with <hi rend="italic">boren</hi>, and from the same root, is the adj. <hi rend="italic">byrde</hi> (‘of high rank’ Sweet <hi rend="italic">Ags. reader;</hi> ‘born’ Bosw.-Toller), which Ælfred likewise uses in the comparative: ‘each pays <hi rend="italic">be hys gebyrdum, se byrdesta</hi> must pay 75’; <hi rend="italic">Oros.</hi> ed. Sweet 18. In Middle High German too <hi rend="italic">geboren</hi> acquires the sense ‘noble, of equal birth’. — The 11th cent. took exception to the word; H cor. alters it to ‘better born’, thus with a double comparative, and So Ld, and perhaps Q’s exemplar, to ‘more nobly born’. Since <hi rend="italic">æðelboren</hi> occurs frequently, earlier editors adopted the latter into the text. — Possibly Af wrote <hi rend="italic">deorborenran,</hi> as in Ine 34, 1, and the archetype, misled by the identical <hi rend="italic">-or</hi>, overlooked the first 4 letters</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_11-5.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vielleicht wuchs die Notzuchtbusse bei der Jungfrau von 600 bzw. 1200 Schill. Wergeld, wie Wilda 837 meint, nur auf 100 bzw. 120 Schill., gemäss der Ehebruchs- und Unzuchtbusse in Af 10. 18, 1, also nicht im Verhältnis des Wergelds (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 21. a; Stand 21s. t) auf 180 bzw. 360 Schill.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps the compensation for rape of a virgin of 600 or 1200 shill. wergild rose, as Wilda 837 thinks, only to 100 or 120 shill. respectively, in line with the compensation for adultery and unchastity in Af 10. 18, 1, and thus not, in proportion to the wergild (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 21. a; Stand 21s. t), to 180 or 360 shill.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_11-5.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>borenran</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">æþelborenran</hi>. So &amp; Ld. <hi rend="italic">bettborenran</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">æðel</hi>. 16th century addition to B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_11-5.attnote.fn.15" n="15" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>weaxe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wexe</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_11-5.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">In H <hi rend="italic">bett</hi> is written above the line, while later MSS read <hi rend="italic">æþel</hi>, which shows that the uncompounded <hi rend="italic">borenran</hi> was not understood in later times. I know of no exact parallel for its use, and it is a question whether some word has not been omitted in the MS from which all our copies are derived (see Liebermann’s note <hi rend="italic">ad loc.</hi>).</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
